size 32 34
tag "Calibration"
tag "Terrain Materials"
description "Terrain Material Calibration: 24 labelled regions A-X, read west to east. Original swatches rows 01-17; cliff bays rows 19-25 and 27-33. Dirt rows 06 and 12 separate bands."
description "A-H: grass, dirt, rock, sand on rock, pavement, snow, lunar, fungus. I-P: desert, Mars, volcanic ground, tropical ground, planted field, reed marsh, mud, tundra."
description "Q-X: quicksand, water, ice over water, magma crust, flowing magma, hazardous liquid, sparse woods, sparse jungle. Dry north/middle regions and both magma regions descend from level 2 to 1 to a level 0 reference area."
description "Selected contacts: grass/dirt; rock/sand; pavement/snow; lunar/fungus; field/marsh; marsh/mud; water/ice; crust/flowing magma. J1 grass-dirt-rock at 0405/0505/0506; J2 tropical-field-dirt at 1611/1711/1712; J3 snow-water-ice at 0812/0813/0913. This is a diagnostic board, not a balanced scenario."
description "Cliff bays C01-C07, columns01-28 rows19-25: grass, dirt, rock, sand on rock, pavement, snow, lunar. C08-C14 rows27-33: fungus, desert, Mars, volcanic ground, tropical, solid magma crust, molten lava fall. Each bay is four columns wide; the first three rows are level4/5/6 and the remaining four level0. These direct drops invoke actual cliffs, not the original two-level banks."
description "Columns29-32: V1 grass/dirt plateaus at6 over rock at0, rows19-25; V2 snow at6 over lunar ground at0, rows27-33. V1 triple contact3021/3121/3122 spans the vertical edge. Rows18/26 and the final toe row34 are dirt at0. No manual cliff_top terrain is used: the game generates high-incline edges and the renderer selects cliffs automatically."
